Title:  Note Link

Seq:    5.5.6

Level:  4 - chunk

Class:  non-version

Timestamp: 20260802163124

Body:

The phrase `note link` can be used as both a label and a type. 

When editing, the user will be presented with a [combo box](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combo_box) allowing a selection of Note titles within the current Collection. 

When displayed, the target Note title will become an active link, allowing the user to click on it in order to be taken to the target. 

Functionally, a `note-link` field behaves similarly to a [[Wiki Style Link]] within a Markdown field, the difference being that the field type is separated from any surrounding text and allowed to stand on its own.

Here is an example of how the defining line might appear within [[the Collection Template File]]:

```
Recording Artist: <notelink>
```

The list of potential target notes may be limited to those of a single [[Class]] by placing the class name following the field type, as in the following example. 

```
Recording Artist: <notelink: artist >
```
